    "mechanism": [
      "New per-statement absence checks are separated from transaction-wide commit flags using the existing undo checkpoint, avoiding rechecking and recopying old INSERT flags.",
      "The worker checks new absence assertions on held keys before filtering acquisitions; the existing lock-value cache supplies existence, with Go's true default for non-returning locks.",
      "Existing lazy normal-INSERT policy propagates to unique indexes via shared Get/GetLocal checking; local duplicate/tombstone behavior and eager conflict-resolution paths remain.",
      "Eager index read failures propagate instead of being treated as absence."
    ],
